Ugly Newt <gkennington@claIrVOYaNT.coLD.DuCk> writes:

> I assume that this is because I changed the size of "struct flag" - do
> other patch-writers get this problem, or have I screwed up?

Changing the size of struct flag is one of the things that also
invalidates existing bones and save files, and that's why many patch
writers try to avoid that.
If you need new runtime options for a patch, adding them to struct
instance_flags instead of flags will keep bones and save files compatible,
but those options are not saved in the save files, they are just read from
the configuration file. For many options this is not a big problem, but
for some others it may be a bad thing, depending on the patch.

